WEBVTT

00:05.422 --> 00:07.424
Hey, Xeno!

00:07.507 --> 00:08.883
Here you are.

00:08.967 --> 00:10.385
It's your lucky day.

00:10.468 --> 00:13.513
You're our first customer
in the New World.

00:16.850 --> 00:19.394
<i>Just like Senku…</i>

00:20.478 --> 00:24.149
<i>No, it's not. This is more refined.</i>

00:26.359 --> 00:28.778
<i>They're skilled scientists…</i>

00:30.655 --> 00:32.365
<i>for real.</i>

00:33.033 --> 00:38.496
&lrm;ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
&lrm;SHUEISHA JUMP COMICS

02:13.049 --> 02:14.217
What is it?

02:14.300 --> 02:17.137
That absurdly tall pole sticking out…

02:17.220 --> 02:20.306
It's impressive.
They're building something

02:20.390 --> 02:21.850
with their scientific knowledge.

02:25.061 --> 02:27.647
We must gather as much info
as possible about the enemy

02:27.730 --> 02:29.691
to report back to Senku and the others.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.362
By the way,

02:34.988 --> 02:36.406
where's Gen?

02:36.489 --> 02:38.825
Did he manage to sneak in safely?

02:40.034 --> 02:43.872
He's a smooth talker,
he's good with words.

02:43.955 --> 02:45.665
I don't think he'll mess up too badly.

02:45.748 --> 02:48.751
<i>He's the most</i>
<i>trustworthy liar in the world.</i>

02:48.835 --> 02:50.628
Smooth as silk.

02:51.212 --> 02:54.632
Can he really be trustworthy and a liar
at the same time?

02:58.887 --> 03:00.597
<i>Perseus, do you copy me?</i>

03:00.680 --> 03:02.765
<i>There's a little change in plan--</i>

03:02.849 --> 03:05.184
Yes, say no more.

03:08.313 --> 03:09.147
<i>What?</i>

03:09.230 --> 03:12.233
I see, it's because this is wireless.

03:13.109 --> 03:15.320
Since our enemies are also scientists,

03:15.403 --> 03:17.488
our communications could be intercepted.

03:17.572 --> 03:21.117
Our movements were too easy
for them to figure out.

03:21.200 --> 03:22.201
True.

03:23.161 --> 03:25.288
The enemy also understands Japanese.

03:25.371 --> 03:27.248
We should take precautions.

03:27.957 --> 03:30.668
Using only the minimum
amount of information,

03:30.752 --> 03:34.255
what's our current status?
Who's there right now?

03:35.590 --> 03:37.425
It's just me and Koha…

03:37.508 --> 03:39.010
the woman, just the two of us.

03:40.094 --> 03:43.431
Option A,
only Gen was taken captive by the enemy.

03:43.514 --> 03:46.601
Option B,
Gen infiltrated pretending to betray us.

03:47.185 --> 03:50.563
It's B. A sailor's intuition
is always spot on.

03:52.398 --> 03:54.400
There's no such thing as intuition here.

03:54.484 --> 03:56.819
I'm ten billion percent sure about it too.

03:58.655 --> 03:59.697
Did you hang up?

04:00.490 --> 04:04.160
They'd locate the source of the signal
if we kept talking for long.

04:04.911 --> 04:08.164
Yes, we don't know
what kind of technology the enemy has.

04:08.998 --> 04:12.210
This is totally different
from any battle we've fought so far.

04:13.211 --> 04:15.922
Science has always been our advantage,

04:16.005 --> 04:17.882
&lrm;but this time,

04:17.966 --> 04:20.802
the enemy might surpass us in that aspect.

04:22.637 --> 04:25.306
So, is this going to be
a science showdown?

04:27.475 --> 04:30.436
This is tempting!

04:35.441 --> 04:36.609
Damn…

04:37.443 --> 04:40.280
What are you doing, Chrome? You, idiot…

04:40.363 --> 04:41.656
We just told you not to call…

04:42.740 --> 04:44.867
<i>Hey, hello there.</i>

04:46.244 --> 04:49.747
I see. So, your communications…

04:50.832 --> 04:53.001
work on this frequency.

04:57.714 --> 05:01.592
<i>Nice to meet you, ladies and gentlemen</i>
<i>of the Little Kingdom of Science.</i>

05:02.385 --> 05:04.220
<i>The enemy contacted us!</i>

05:08.099 --> 05:09.809
So you're the bad guy, aren't you?

05:09.892 --> 05:11.853
You've got guts!

05:12.437 --> 05:14.689
Excuse my poor Japanese,

05:14.772 --> 05:17.317
but this isn't something
an idiot would understand.

05:18.568 --> 05:20.278
<i>I'm Dr. Xeno.</i>

05:20.361 --> 05:23.281
<i>I'd like to speak to your science leader.</i>

05:25.283 --> 05:27.744
Let me speak to Dr. Taiju.

05:31.581 --> 05:34.208
-Dr. Taiju?
-Dr. Taiju?

05:35.918 --> 05:36.753
Me?

05:39.213 --> 05:40.381
Surely this is Gen's doing.

05:41.924 --> 05:44.969
Did he use our toughest guy as a decoy?

05:45.053 --> 05:47.555
He'll be the bodyguard for our scientist.

05:47.638 --> 05:48.556
Well done!

05:48.639 --> 05:51.434
What? So that's what it is!

06:02.987 --> 06:05.823
In that case, I'll take this fight!

06:06.407 --> 06:09.035
Is the costume necessary?
It's only a phone call.

06:09.118 --> 06:10.953
Everything starts with appearance.

06:12.246 --> 06:15.416
Taiju speaking. Dr. Taiju.

06:15.500 --> 06:17.460
&lrm;And you're Dr. Xeno, right?

06:17.543 --> 06:20.463
&lrm;I have something to tell you first,
&lrm;so listen up.

06:21.047 --> 06:23.966
It's not good to suddenly shoot people

06:24.050 --> 06:25.593
with a machine gun!

06:26.677 --> 06:28.262
<i>-Well, sure…</i>
<i>-Well, sure…</i>

06:28.763 --> 06:30.598
Yeah, sorry about that.

06:30.681 --> 06:32.934
My soldier here, Stanley,

06:33.017 --> 06:35.019
was only trying to greet you…

06:36.521 --> 06:39.482
by showing how we're worlds apart
in terms of scientific prowess.

06:41.484 --> 06:45.446
Being a scientist yourself, Dr. Taiju,
I'm sure you understand

06:45.530 --> 06:46.739
what this means.

06:47.532 --> 06:51.536
We've just built a Haber-Bosch plant.

06:52.120 --> 06:53.371
What?

06:54.163 --> 06:57.542
A Ha-- Haberdoe… something!

06:57.625 --> 06:59.794
That's impressive, Dr. Xeno!

06:59.877 --> 07:03.005
<i>Don't talk that much, you big oaf…</i>

07:03.089 --> 07:04.799
<i>You’ll give away the whole game!</i>

07:04.882 --> 07:08.261
Hey, what is that Haber-something thing?

07:08.928 --> 07:11.139
A Haber-Bosch plant.

07:11.222 --> 07:13.015
It's an ammonia chemical plant.

07:13.891 --> 07:15.143
Simply put,

07:16.352 --> 07:18.354
<i>they can produce huge amounts…</i>

07:18.438 --> 07:21.315
<i>no, actually, infinite amounts</i>
<i>of gunpowder from just water and air.</i>

07:21.399 --> 07:23.776
<i>In other words, bullets.</i>

07:24.819 --> 07:25.862
I see!

07:25.945 --> 07:31.033
So that means that you can fire
an infinite amount of machine gun rounds!

07:31.784 --> 07:34.370
As expected, you're quick to catch things,

07:34.454 --> 07:35.455
Dr. Taiju.

07:36.456 --> 07:38.583
<i>-As if he knew all along!</i>
<i>-As if he knew all along!</i>

07:39.375 --> 07:41.836
Taiju's acting skills
are surprisingly good.

07:41.919 --> 07:44.130
I don't think he's actually acting…

07:44.964 --> 07:47.592
We're a refined, professional team,

07:47.675 --> 07:51.637
leagues above your little
make-believe science club.

07:52.221 --> 07:56.100
We want you to surrender
and serve us willingly.

07:56.184 --> 07:57.685
That's all.

07:57.768 --> 08:00.188
<i>We're short on manpower.</i>

08:01.272 --> 08:03.524
What did he say?

08:03.608 --> 08:05.443
"Short on manpower"?

08:05.526 --> 08:08.946
Why didn't they just revive
the stone statues lying around there?

08:10.740 --> 08:14.285
That means, they don't know anything
about the Revival Fluid, do they?

08:16.496 --> 08:20.875
That's because that's the only bit
of science that isn't common knowledge.

08:21.876 --> 08:24.337
The only humans who can be revived
by being poured nitric acid

08:24.420 --> 08:28.508
are those who stayed conscious during
petrification for thousands of years.

08:29.425 --> 08:32.720
We are the chosen ones
who have accomplished that.

08:34.430 --> 08:36.807
However, there's a few of you.

08:37.308 --> 08:39.769
It's hard to believe all of you,

08:39.852 --> 08:43.773
such young kids, have accomplished that.

08:44.440 --> 08:46.609
<i>How did you get depetrified?</i>

08:47.652 --> 08:49.278
Well, about that…

08:51.072 --> 08:54.283
The Revival Fluid is our only advantage.

08:54.367 --> 08:55.743
We're not giving it away.

08:56.369 --> 08:58.788
They introduced themselves
with machine guns.

08:59.622 --> 09:02.250
If we tell them, we'll be crushed
by a huge army in no time.

09:02.833 --> 09:05.002
Yes, if they discover the recipe,

09:05.086 --> 09:08.589
they'll be able to make
as much as they want.

09:09.549 --> 09:11.801
They have nitric acid at their plant,

09:11.884 --> 09:14.136
along with alcohol from the corn.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.305
In other words,

09:16.389 --> 09:19.767
if we get our hands on those,
we'll be done with this corn city.

09:20.518 --> 09:25.523
Then we'll just have to make
the Revival Fluid for billions of people.

09:26.816 --> 09:30.653
We refuse to teach you
how to make our Revival Fluid!

09:32.947 --> 09:36.659
<i>I see. Negotiations are over, then.</i>

09:37.785 --> 09:39.120
<i>What a pity…</i>

09:58.806 --> 10:00.766
<i>This is terrible!</i>

10:00.850 --> 10:03.603
<i>That plane is coming again!</i>

10:15.448 --> 10:17.700
That's quite a huge mothership.

10:17.783 --> 10:20.911
They've found us.
They've located the Perseus!

10:20.995 --> 10:23.998
What, they have more aircraft?

10:24.081 --> 10:26.417
Why would you think they only had one?

10:31.088 --> 10:32.715
Was that merely a reconnaisance?

10:33.549 --> 10:36.886
I guess they won't be flying
as dangerously low as they did

10:36.969 --> 10:39.472
when they chased us by the river before.

10:40.890 --> 10:44.268
But then, we won't be able
to hit them with our spears and arrows.

10:44.852 --> 10:47.855
How do we fight an opponent
with an airplane, Senku?

10:49.398 --> 10:52.360
Well, we have an airplane too.

10:52.443 --> 10:54.445
The one we borrowed.

10:56.364 --> 10:58.741
I can't wait to have it fixed!

10:58.824 --> 11:00.534
Aren't you also excited

11:00.618 --> 11:02.495
with a machine like this?

11:05.373 --> 11:08.959
But, how can we make it fly?

11:09.710 --> 11:12.004
Unlike the enemy, we have no runway here…

11:13.547 --> 11:14.924
So, we'll make one.

11:15.007 --> 11:16.467
-Where?
-Where?

11:17.510 --> 11:18.511
Right here.

11:20.221 --> 11:22.139
We'll make an aircraft carrier!

11:22.223 --> 11:24.725
We’ll begin with the big remodeling plan

11:24.809 --> 11:26.143
for Perseus!

11:32.733 --> 11:34.652
We got this!

11:36.987 --> 11:39.031
An aircraft carrier?

11:48.040 --> 11:49.083
Hey!

11:49.166 --> 11:51.877
Let's review our battle situation!

11:54.713 --> 11:57.174
Here comes the nice Magma.

11:57.258 --> 12:01.387
The way you speak is overly polite,
it makes me cringe.

12:01.470 --> 12:04.765
Shut up and listen, or I'll kill you.

12:04.849 --> 12:07.476
Your mask came off
in just about five seconds.

12:07.560 --> 12:09.145
Try a bit harder!

12:09.812 --> 12:11.605
I'll tear him apart!

12:11.689 --> 12:13.441
That damn Dr. Xeno…

12:14.150 --> 12:16.652
We came to get some corn,

12:16.735 --> 12:19.780
and the one who has it is Dr. Xeno.

12:19.864 --> 12:22.199
I'm still deciding what to do with him.

12:22.283 --> 12:23.159
&lrm;KILL

12:23.242 --> 12:25.369
What do you mean by that?

12:25.953 --> 12:27.621
What I want, Yo,

12:27.705 --> 12:29.623
is that gun on your waist, bastard.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.585
Yay!

12:32.668 --> 12:35.337
This isn't some kind
of rampage or anything,

12:35.421 --> 12:38.299
but it's a real maneuver!

12:38.382 --> 12:40.759
We'll get it done quick.

12:40.843 --> 12:44.305
<i>If we succeed, we'll be immortalized</i>

12:44.388 --> 12:46.640
<i>as the heroes who saved everyone!</i>

12:46.724 --> 12:48.017
HEROES

12:54.398 --> 12:56.275
Let's go finish Xeno!

12:59.570 --> 13:00.571
No way…

13:11.874 --> 13:13.417
What kind of idiots are you?

13:13.501 --> 13:17.004
Were you really thinking about charging
head-on against a machine gun?

13:17.087 --> 13:19.507
We've got guns too!

13:19.590 --> 13:22.843
The difference in firepower
is on a scale of ten billion.

13:22.927 --> 13:25.679
We'll start building the gunpowder
factory, even if it takes time.

13:25.763 --> 13:29.141
But if the enemy were waiting for us,
that'd be a whole different story…

13:32.686 --> 13:33.896
Now,

13:33.979 --> 13:36.190
let's review our battle situation.

13:37.483 --> 13:39.693
<i>He said exactly what Magma said,</i>

13:39.777 --> 13:41.946
<i>yet he sounded more trustworthy.</i>

13:50.913 --> 13:53.457
It looks like a board game!

13:53.541 --> 13:55.834
Are we going to play it?

13:56.669 --> 13:57.836
KOHAKU, XENO

13:57.920 --> 13:59.088
GEN

13:59.672 --> 14:01.423
-A war council?
-Yes.

14:02.216 --> 14:05.511
First, let's clarify our army's position
relative to the enemy's.

14:06.762 --> 14:10.307
At this moment, we are right here.

14:13.686 --> 14:16.188
-Do we know where the enemy's base is?
-Yes.

14:17.314 --> 14:20.901
We can use the the radio signal direction
and the timing of Chrome's contact

14:21.527 --> 14:22.736
to estimate the distance.

14:25.155 --> 14:26.699
It's probably over here.

14:28.576 --> 14:31.036
Yes, the enemy base is very close.

14:31.120 --> 14:32.955
Now that makes sense.

14:33.038 --> 14:34.707
But…

14:34.790 --> 14:37.084
they've discovered our position too!

14:37.167 --> 14:40.379
Wouldn't it be better
if we just fled with Perseus?

14:40.963 --> 14:43.048
It’s pointless
if the enemy has patrol planes.

14:43.716 --> 14:47.595
If we limit ourselves to the sea,
we'll lose all escape routes through land.

14:47.678 --> 14:50.973
Sure! That's what I thought too.

14:51.640 --> 14:54.476
Hyoga, if you were our enemy…

14:54.560 --> 14:56.979
if you were Dr. Xeno, what would you do?

14:57.980 --> 15:00.232
I would build a pirate ship.

15:03.152 --> 15:05.946
If the enemy knows what the right move is…

15:06.530 --> 15:08.490
Since the difference
in firearms is so clear,

15:08.574 --> 15:11.285
they could approach us
with fast, small boats

15:11.368 --> 15:13.287
and seize control at once.

15:16.582 --> 15:19.460
A big ship like this
wouldn't be able to escape.

15:20.044 --> 15:21.128
It's the same tactic

15:21.629 --> 15:24.298
that real, modern-day pirates use.

15:26.842 --> 15:31.764
Thanks to the patrol plane,
they’ve pinpointed Perseus's location

15:32.348 --> 15:34.058
<i>and can attack us from above.</i>

15:36.518 --> 15:40.189
It doesn't matter
how strong we are in close combat…

15:43.609 --> 15:45.569
We can't take to the skies.

15:48.530 --> 15:51.825
In a battle where one side
commands air superiority,

15:51.909 --> 15:53.494
we don't stand a chance.

15:55.120 --> 15:58.457
Exactly! In other words,
if we had a plane too…

15:59.792 --> 16:00.960
<i>That'd be a dogfight!</i>

16:01.543 --> 16:03.128
<i>Let’s take the fight to the skies!</i>

16:05.589 --> 16:07.508
A dogfight?

16:08.092 --> 16:11.053
Yes, and for that purpose…

16:23.190 --> 16:26.110
Let's build our aircraft carrier, Perseus!

16:27.736 --> 16:30.656
Let’s kick off our all-out factory!

16:56.015 --> 16:57.474
Impressive!

16:57.558 --> 17:00.269
They really are building
a runway on the deck.

17:01.478 --> 17:03.522
Will it really fly with this?

17:05.482 --> 17:07.359
If it's an ultra-light plane,

17:07.443 --> 17:10.320
the take-off distance
is only about 20 meters.

17:10.404 --> 17:11.405
Exactly.

17:11.488 --> 17:14.867
And we can land by catching a wire
and coming to a forceful stop.

17:14.950 --> 17:17.119
Just like a real aircraft carrier.

17:17.703 --> 17:21.123
That will do! I was also thinking
about who should be the pilot.

17:21.206 --> 17:23.834
I'm going to modify the aircraft too.

17:23.917 --> 17:26.879
It's way faster
than building it from scratch.

17:26.962 --> 17:28.130
Your eyes again!

17:28.213 --> 17:30.591
Your mask came off in five seconds!

17:30.674 --> 17:33.427
You just want to build
the aircraft carrier, don't you?

17:38.015 --> 17:40.726
If we're going to run an airplane
on a wooden runway,

17:40.809 --> 17:44.146
we should first change the wheels
to the familiar bamboo ones.

17:44.229 --> 17:45.606
Leave that to me!

17:47.983 --> 17:50.944
Did you bring that bamboo
all the way from Japan?

17:51.028 --> 17:52.321
Yes.

17:52.404 --> 17:54.990
Bamboo is our one secret material

17:55.074 --> 17:57.451
that gives us a slight edge.

17:58.077 --> 17:59.286
I see!

17:59.369 --> 18:00.954
Bamboo doesn't naturally grow in America.

18:02.956 --> 18:06.043
That's why the enemy's airplane
has these grass skis

18:06.126 --> 18:07.711
instead of wheels.

18:07.795 --> 18:09.588
With those skis,

18:09.671 --> 18:14.426
there's a slim chance of landing
anywhere other than the cornfield runway.

18:15.552 --> 18:17.262
He's a smart guy, after all…

18:17.846 --> 18:19.765
When he realized he lacked the materials,

18:19.848 --> 18:21.975
he designed an improved version.

18:24.061 --> 18:26.230
This enemy seems hard to beat!

18:27.815 --> 18:29.233
<i>Dr. Xeno…</i>

18:34.988 --> 18:36.782
What's wrong, Ryusui?

18:36.865 --> 18:39.743
Nothing…
It's just that Dr. Xeno is a sharp one.

18:40.452 --> 18:42.538
<i>A pilot like me can recognize the way</i>

18:42.621 --> 18:44.790
<i>that patrol aircraft was flying.</i>

18:44.873 --> 18:48.752
<i>He was trying to show us</i>
<i>that there's nowhere to escape.</i>

18:48.836 --> 18:50.254
Or, perhaps,

18:50.337 --> 18:52.881
he was trying to pin us down here.

18:53.674 --> 18:56.301
A sailor's intuition is always spot on!

19:03.142 --> 19:04.893
The patrol aircraft went to confirm…

19:06.436 --> 19:09.106
that they couldn't escape.

19:21.410 --> 19:27.499
Are we going to chase them down
in our planes and take them out by force?

19:29.084 --> 19:32.504
Those poor kids… the smarter they are,

19:32.588 --> 19:35.883
the warier they get,
thus leaving them unable to act.

19:36.466 --> 19:37.718
However,

19:37.801 --> 19:41.638
we could actually find a more elegant way.

19:44.766 --> 19:48.937
We could just corner
the enemy scientist and kill him.

19:49.980 --> 19:52.191
Kill him?

19:52.274 --> 19:55.444
According to this guy over here, Mr. Gen,

19:55.527 --> 19:57.738
they have a single genius scientist.

19:58.322 --> 19:59.448
If that's the case,

19:59.948 --> 20:03.243
we just need to get rid of that leader

20:04.286 --> 20:07.873
to destroy the Little Kingdom of Science.

20:11.501 --> 20:13.462
<i>That Dr. Taiju.</i>

20:15.923 --> 20:18.592
That's smart, for real…

20:18.675 --> 20:21.386
But can you do that?

20:27.768 --> 20:28.894
Of course.

20:32.064 --> 20:33.690
How?

20:35.234 --> 20:36.610
We simply can.

20:38.362 --> 20:39.905
Oh, Mr. Gen.

20:40.405 --> 20:42.407
If Stan says he can,

20:42.491 --> 20:45.410
there's no need to ask any further.

20:47.246 --> 20:49.081
He can do it.

20:50.624 --> 20:55.087
<i>I'm so sorry, dear Taiju…</i>

20:56.129 --> 20:58.382
If we just abandon Gen, Chrome and Kohaku,

20:58.966 --> 21:01.468
forget about the corn,

21:01.551 --> 21:04.221
and flee all the way to the ocean,
we might save ourselves.

21:04.304 --> 21:06.807
We can't do that!

21:06.890 --> 21:08.600
I thought so…

21:08.684 --> 21:11.270
But the enemy doesn't know that.

21:11.353 --> 21:13.272
That's my main point.

21:13.355 --> 21:16.358
That's why they'll act quickly
and hit us with a fast attack.

21:18.277 --> 21:20.153
Then, as a generous gesture,

21:20.237 --> 21:23.824
why don't we strike first
with a quick attack?

21:25.450 --> 21:29.955
A small attack unit will capture Dr. Xeno,

21:30.038 --> 21:32.374
the enemy source of science.

21:32.958 --> 21:34.167
The members will be

21:36.295 --> 21:39.464
Tsukasa, Hyoga, Ukyo,

21:39.548 --> 21:41.133
and lastly…

21:42.551 --> 21:44.928
-Suika!
-Me?

21:46.305 --> 21:48.932
<i>None of them can move their main forces.</i>

21:49.516 --> 21:51.018
<i>There's no escape.</i>

21:51.101 --> 21:55.272
<i>We've been scientifically beseiged</i>
<i>into a brawl.</i>

21:55.856 --> 21:57.190
<i>In that case,</i>

21:58.567 --> 22:00.068
<i>the one who checkmates</i>

22:00.152 --> 22:02.946
<i>the enemy science leader</i>
<i>at their main base, wins.</i>

22:08.035 --> 22:11.121
<i>Two Kingdoms of Science</i>
<i>are going to duke it out…</i>

22:12.873 --> 22:14.583
<i>in a quick-strike battle!</i>

